Test same-density LDA/PBE direct paired labels for the multi-k H2O molecule.
PBE drives SCF; the label-only LDA evaluation must not change the active result.
The historical directory name is retained to preserve case numbering.
Paired arrays use OUT.autotest/deepks_sample_*.npy and deepks_pair_*.npy.

The ordinary Hamiltonian reference now matches pair-disabled SCF. The retired
output path refreshed the active Hamiltonian at the output density as a side
effect. Paired delta-E/delta-H samples retain their previous numerical values.
The stress-operator checksum was checked against a separate HEAD build: the
previous result.ref value was already stale before this refactor.
Final paired force/virial labels are fixed-density derivative differences;
they are not legacy auxiliary forces with an SCF charge-correction term.
